% ============================================================================
% moon-phase-ordinal-position.query.adj — worked recall over the moon-phase/
% ordinal bridge library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what place is this Moon
% phase in the cycle, in words?" — it states no fact of its own — it only
% `import`s the grounded rule and asks binding queries. The answer is
% DERIVED, joining a moon-phase-order fact to an ordinal-word fact, so every
% answer carries BOTH citations in its `steps` trail.
%
% Placed at the stdlib PACKAGE ROOT (not beside `astronomy/moon-phase-
% ordinal-position.adj`) — the same cross-directory-import sandboxing
% pattern `astronomy/planet-ordinal-position.adj` (and, before it,
% `earth-science/season-start-month-number.adj`) already established: the
% library itself lives in `astronomy/` and reaches its mathematics sibling
% via a relative `../mathematics/ordinal-numbers.adj` import, which only
% resolves if the CONSUMING entry program (this file) sits at or above the
% package root.
%
% Run (from this directory, the package root, so the relative import
% resolves):
%     ../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli moon-phase-ordinal-position.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "astronomy/moon-phase-ordinal-position.adj"

? moon_phase_ordinal_position(full_moon, $O)      % expect fifth  (direct: what place is the full Moon in the cycle, in words?)
? moon_phase_ordinal_position($P, eighth)         % expect waning_crescent (reverse: which phase is eighth?)
? moon_phase_ordinal_position(eclipse, $O)        % expect abstain -- an eclipse is not one of the 8 lunar phases tabled
